7] [17592186129259 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129259 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186371865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129259 #edb/ref 1039 "Applying the Product Rule and Swap Rules" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129259 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186128835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129259 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "08375770-c610-5dae-b01b-c457de086cba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129331 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129331 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129331 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129331 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129331 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129331 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129331 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129331 #edb/ref 1045 "Double Summations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129331 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186130036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129331 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129331 #edb/ref 1050 600.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129331 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "b93dfde4-f3d0-56f7-90c3-7b5628613c8b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129499 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129499 #edb/ref 1069 "q-149600" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129499 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129499 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}4({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}{a}_{ij}=40,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}{b}_{ij}=60.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129499 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d34efdb1-67e3-5372-9a9f-94c6cc6bc5be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129499 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129499 #edb/ref 1074 "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying these rules to the given sum, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}4({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & =4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) \\\\  & =4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}{a}_{ij}+4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 40+4\\cdot 60 \\\\  & =160+240 \\\\  & =400.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129850 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129850 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72094" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129850 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129850 #edb/ref 1071 "${\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}ij=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129850 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6e16a192-c647-58f3-9bd2-bc5597aebc2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129850 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}ij & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}ij] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}(1j+2j+3j) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}(j+2j+3j) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}6j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}6j & =6\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6+12 \\\\  & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130035 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130035 #edb/ref 1061 22705 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130035 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ac75c745-5dbd-5824-9f7d-04a8faf6a86c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130035 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130036 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130036 #edb/ref 1061 22707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130036 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "583e493e-9206-508f-b782-7eec0883a7d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130036 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130037 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130037 #edb/ref 1061 22708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130037 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3d0a00d2-9ccc-5261-bfa0-15e1bf5cb3c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130037 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130038 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130038 #edb/ref 1061 22710 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130038 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "42e12d98-e4bf-512d-b3c2-5c93584fc740" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130038 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130195 #edb/ref 1061 39727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130195 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4e8c00d9-bc34-56d4-a71a-61e0e176e8fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130195 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129259 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130196 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130196 #edb/ref 1061 39728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130196 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5a28b905-cf2f-59e1-aaa2-6fb0064fcd4b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130196 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130377 #edb/ref 1064 "Recall that we use **sigma notation** to write sums concisely. For example, \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^n a_i\n$$\n\nrefers to the sum of all terms in the sequence $a_i,$ where the **index** $i$ ranges from $1$ to $n\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^n a_i = a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_n\n$$\n\nSigma notation can also represent sums whose terms depend on two indices. That is, **double sums** of the form \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m \\sum_{j=1}^n a_{ij}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $i$ ranges from $1$ to $m,$ and $j$ ranges from $1$ to $n\\mathbin.$ Thus, a double summation is just a \"sum of a sum.\" \n\nIn calculating double summations, we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we evaluate the inner sum by fixing the index of the outer sum ($i$) and incrementing only the inner index ($j$).\n\n- Next, we evaluate the outer sum by incrementing the outer sum index.\n\nTo illustrate how it works, suppose we are given the following double sum:\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^2 \\sum_{j=1}^4 (i+j)\n$$\n\n \n\nTo compute this double sum, we can proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{4}(i+j) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}[({\\sum }_{j=1}^{4}(i+j))] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}[(i+1)+(i+2)+(i+3)+(i+4)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(4i+10) \\\\  & =4(1)+10+4(2)+10 \\\\  & =4+10+8+10 \\\\  & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLater, we will provide some formulas that will help us simplify many double summations calculations." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130377 #edb/ref 1065 3867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130377 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3c842b98-cbdf-55a4-96a1-360697763430" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130377 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130378 #edb/ref 1064 "Double summations satisfy the following properties:\n\n**The Constant Multiple Rule** \n\nWe can factor out a constant multiple from a double summation:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n k a_{ij} = k\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n a_{ij}\n$$\n\n**The Sum Rule** \n\nWe can distribute a double summation over a sum of terms.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n (a_{ij} + b_{ij}) = \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n a_{ij} + \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n b_{ij}\n$$\n\n**The Double Sum of Units**\n\nRecall that for single summations, we have\n\n$$\n\\sum_{j=1}^{n} 1 = \\underbrace{1+1+\\cdots+1}_{n\\textrm{ times}}  = n.\n$$\n\nAnalogously for double summations, we have that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n 1 = mn.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130378 #edb/ref 1065 3868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130378 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "41df0fcf-551a-58a5-b47e-ac1ddd121f7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130378 #edb/ref 1067 "The Sum and Constant Multiple Rules" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130453 #edb/ref 1064 "In addition, we have the following useful rules:\n\n**The Product Rule** \n\nWe can distribute a double summation over a product of *single-index* terms with *different* indices.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n  a_{i}b_j = \\sum_{i=1}^m a_i \\sum_{j=1}^n b_{j}\n$$\n\n**The Swap Rule** \n\nWe can swap the order of summations in a double summation.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n a_{ij}= \\sum_{j=1}^n\\sum_{i=1}^m a_{ij}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130453 #edb/ref 1065 6584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130453 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d25ceabe-e67a-59b3-9ed6-37be45644e5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130453 #edb/ref 1067 "The Product and Swap Rules" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272663 #edb/ref 1080 "65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272663 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272663 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1f564799-072a-59cc-96e5-da621926444a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272821 #edb/ref 1080 "75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272821 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272821 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "30d49607-ca61-5e6a-9a58-381e5e653ae6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273928 #edb/ref 1080 "70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273928 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273928 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b241ab01-5e9b-57e2-b39d-41a0df962b2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274262 #edb/ref 1080 "80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274262 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274262 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d649f46b-6f36-5773-9cfd-5caf55c72157" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274592 #edb/ref 1080 "60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274592 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274592 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fb661a82-596b-553a-8787-25455a66aa3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274735 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186272663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274735 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186272821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274735 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274735 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274735 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274735 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274735 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274735 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186273928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274735 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3837bfb6-67dd-5e82-82e3-c2662a455ffd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275228 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275228 #edb/ref 1069 "q-149676" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275228 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275228 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}-2)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}{a}_{ij}=300,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}{b}_{ij}=250.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275228 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f734ef27-c15e-5fba-9fca-e94f9a86d030" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275228 #edb/ref 1074 "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}-2) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}{b}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}2 \\\\  & =300+250-(2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}1) \\\\  & =550-2({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}1=mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}550-2({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}1) & =550-2\\cdot (15\\cdot 16) \\\\  & =550-480 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}-2)=70.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336086 #edb/ref 1080 "11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336086 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336086 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0735a4cd-515a-5587-aec7-e76fddc755c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336174 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336174 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336174 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0ee3daa0-63ea-57fd-8203-29e8ffd77480" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336210 #edb/ref 1080 "16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336210 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336210 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "12b2522f-4758-5d90-8080-b542234b7547" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336577 #edb/ref 1080 "18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336577 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336577 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "39fbd0e6-1e9a-5d05-a795-60d8cfddca47" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336820 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336820 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336820 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "55d93502-79ac-5c15-ae2a-e11